    {
      "bonus_rolls": 0.0,
      "rolls": 1.0,
      "entries": [
        {
          "type": "minecraft:item",
          "name": "minecraft:written_book",
          "weight": 1,
          "functions": [
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_count",
              "count": 1.0,
              "add": false
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_book_cover",
              "title": "Hymnal of the Sunken Choir",
              "author": "Wren of the Listeners",
              "generation": 0
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_written_book_pages",
              "pages": [
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "Hymnal of the Sunken Choir",
                    "bold": true,
                    "color": "dark_aqua"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\n\nCopied in the water-library of the Sunken Choir, in the 1104th year of the Chord.",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "I. For the Lighting of Lanterns",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nHold the note, and the crystal wakes.\nHold it long, and the crystal keeps it.\nWhat is sung is never lost."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "II. For the Crossing of Water",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nThe Vesper carries our voices out to the Shallows. Sing low over deep water, so that the deep water knows you."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "III. For the Four Voices",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nSoprano keeps watch.\nAlto welcomes.\nTenor carries.\nBass holds.\nAnd the Heart holds all of us."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "IV. For Those Who Rest",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nRest is not an ending. A silence in the music is still the music. We sing around the rest, and it becomes part of the song."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "(The last hymn is water-stained. Only its refrain can still be read.)",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  },
                  "\n\nListen first.\nListen first.\nListen, and you are never alone in the Hush."
                ]
              ],
              "mode": "replace_all"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "minecraft:item",
          "name": "minecraft:written_book",
          "weight": 1,
          "functions": [
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_count",
              "count": 1.0,
              "add": false
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_book_cover",
              "title": "On the Silent Warden",
              "author": "Wren of the Listeners",
              "generation": 0
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_written_book_pages",
              "pages": [
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "On the Silent Warden",
                    "bold": true,
                    "color": "dark_aqua"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\n\nAs recorded by the Listeners in the 1131st year of the Chord.",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  }
                ],
                "The Wardens were grown in the song to hear a false note and silence it. They have no eyes. They never needed eyes: they see by listening, as we are taught to.",
                "In the years of the Souring the tuners heard a second note under ours. So the Keeper chose one Warden, the oldest and the stillest, to guard the vaults.",
                "It was told: let nothing pass that is not the Chord. It bowed its great head and went down into the dark beneath the echo cores, and it did not come back up.",
                "They call it the Silent Warden because it does not cry out when it hunts. The others roar. This one only listens, and waits, and is never wrong.",
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "If you read this in the Hush, do not break what it guards.",
                    "color": "dark_red"
                  },
                  "\n\nIt is not cruel. It is keeping a promise that no one is left to release it from."
                ]
              ],
              "mode": "replace_all"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "minecraft:item",
          "name": "minecraft:written_book",
          "weight": 1,
          "functions": [
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_count",
              "count": 1.0,
              "add": false
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_book_cover",
              "title": "The First Listening",
              "author": "Wren of the Listeners",
              "generation": 0
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_written_book_pages",
              "pages": [
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "The First Listening",
                    "bold": true,
                    "color": "dark_aqua"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\n\nThe oldest story of the Choir, as it is told to small voices.",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  }
                ],
                "Before the Choir, before the Heart, there were only caves in the deep dark of the world above, and people who were afraid of the quiet.",
                "One of them sang into a hollow of amethyst to keep up her courage. The stone sang back, brighter than she had sung. She sang again, and again it answered.",
                "She called the others, and they listened a long while. That night they learned the first truth: stone takes a held note, and remembers it.",
                "So the listening became singing, and the singing became building. We raised halls tuned like instruments. The world above calls them the ancient cities.",
                "In one of them the tuners set deepslate in a frame and struck it with a frozen echo. It opened onto a world where no sound ever fades.\n\nWe named it the Hush."
              ],
              "mode": "replace_all"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "minecraft:item",
          "name": "minecraft:written_book",
          "weight": 1,
          "functions": [
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_count",
              "count": 1.0,
              "add": false
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_book_cover",
              "title": "Resonance: A Treatise",
              "author": "Wren of the Listeners",
              "generation": 0
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_written_book_pages",
              "pages": [
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "Resonance: A Treatise",
                    "bold": true,
                    "color": "dark_aqua"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\n\nOn the nature of the held note. For students of the Tuners.",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  }
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "I. Sound is a shape.",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nA note held long and pure enough shapes whatever hears it. Stone is sung smooth, crystal grows along the chord, water learns to glow."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "II. Light is song made visible.",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nA lantern does not burn. It remembers a note and lets it go slowly, as a lung lets go of a breath."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "III. On echo shards.",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nA shard is an echo so pure it set solid: the note, frozen. That is why a shard opens a gate. A gate is only a note held open."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "IV. On resonite.",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nOre that lay in the song for centuries carries a chord without tiring. Make conduits of it, and cages for lanterns. Never for voices."
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "V. On the Heart.",
                    "color": "dark_purple"
                  },
                  "\n\nThe Heart holds one note, the Undying Chord, and all Aurelith hangs from it: lanterns, river, gates. Tune it gently. Everything listens."
                ]
              ],
              "mode": "replace_all"
            }
          ]
        },
