            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_book_cover",
              "title": "Where the Sculk Began",
              "author": "Wren of the Listeners",
              "generation": 0
            },
            {
              "function": "minecraft:set_written_book_pages",
              "pages": [
                [
                  "",
                  {
                    "text": "Where the Sculk Began",
                    "bold": true,
                    "color": "dark_aqua"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\n\nWritten after the Great Rest, by one who did not walk in the Last Procession.",
                    "italic": true,
                    "color": "dark_gray"
                  }
                ],
                "In C. 1147 Ysolde stood at the Podium and silenced the Heart. I heard the Chord end. I had heard it every day of my life. The quiet after it was enormous.",
                "The Procession left through the gates that night. I stayed to finish the copying. I told myself it was for the books.",
                "On the ninth day something dark and soft was growing in the Heart's shadow, on the stones where the Chord had been loudest. It had small bright mouths. It was listening.",
                "It is not rot, and it is not stone. It grows toward any sound. I think it is the Hush itself, listening for the song that stopped. It does not know the song is gone.",
                "It has reached the Shallows. It has gone through the gates, into the deep dark of the world above. The Wardens did not stop it. It is not a false note. It is no note at all.",
                "The lanterns still burn. Ysolde still stands at the Podium, though the sculk has her now, and she has begun, very softly, to sing again.\n\nI am going to listen."
              ],
              "mode": "replace_all"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
